GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC11): the steady overworld clips with a guard band. A polygon cut
at the picture's edge gets new corners there, on whole pixels, while its own corners land between
pixels, so its texture mapping changed a little as it slid past the edge: texels near the edges
(trees, the ground) jumped a pixel now and then. With a full-screen viewport and the steady
overworld on, the x and y planes are 64 pixels past the picture and the rasterizer trims to the
pixel (corners past the picture are kept signed; polygons from above the screen start their edges
at its first line); box tests keep the exact frustum, so the game culls as it always did.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

